    "description": "On borg-reborn-rs main e0aa2e0a with healing speed 66, which healing curve scale (50, 100, 200 percent) and healing reserve (0, 200, 400 percent of max HP) should the town planner use? Generated from definitions/reborn-heal-curve-small.yaml: 9 arms on 4.2.6-reborn-rust-main-e0aa2e0a, suite classes-1800-small.",
    "issue": 192,
    "name": "reborn-heal-curve-small",
    "owner_authorization": "2026-11-17: after the #192 small tier (run 44116104222) and the reserve x speed pilot (run 44119472667), the owner noted the healing curve scale had never been varied and asked to propose reserve {0, 200, 400} x curve {50, 100, 200} at speed 66, on the small tier's specimen so its arms can be compared. The owner had the pilot run first (reborn-heal-curve-pilot, run 44125061301, gate passed), then asked for small and medium together (2026-11-17).",
    "prespecified": "Fixed 2026-11-17, before any result was read (borg-zoo#192). Small tier, dispatched together with the medium\ntier on the owner's request; the pilot (run 44125061301) came first (RULES 16). The curve scale stretches the town planner's diminishing healing curve: weight and\ndemand scale together, so the first HP keeps its value and the half-value point moves to the scale's\npercent of today's (50 = stops buying healing sooner, 200 = keeps buying). Gate: no config_error; one\nbinary; the three borg_param_town_heal_* lines with the arm's values (reserve 0/200/400, curve\n50/100/200, speed 66) in every arm's borg.txt and in params-core.json of the death replays; no plan\nloaded; every cell ends in death, turn_cap or borg_stopped; frozen-turn stalls and key outliers listed;\ndeath bundles reproduced. Consistency check: r0-c100, r200-c100 and r400-c100 are the arms r0, r200 and\nr400 of reborn-heal-reserve-s66-small (same specimen, same starts, same values) and should reproduce\ntheir key hashes; any difference is reported before anything else. Report per arm: deaths, final level,\ndeepest level, keys; deaths by class, with low-max-HP casters (Mage, Necromancer) called out; paired\nrescued and newly killed against r0-c100 on the same start, with an exact McNemar p; per reserve, the\nsame against its own c100 arm; healing potions bought (Cure Light/Serious/Critical Wounds, Healing),\nPhase Door bought, and gold on each against all gold spent, from all games where the run records\npurchases, else from the death replays (say which). Watch the Phase Door crowding a local simulation\nfound (borg-reborn-rs, 18 starts: departures with no Phase Door 38 at r0 against 114 at r400-c100,\nconcentrated in Warrior 1019921749 and Ranger 1739161339): does c50 reduce it? r400-c100 is the shipped\nvalue. 90 starts per arm show direction, not a confirmed difference.",
